<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2>What engineers ask about the record.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Can we start from our current CMMS or ERP?</summary>
        <div><p>Yes. Bulk-import existing records, or build the register directly. Attributes come pre-configured for each equipment type, so you add, remove, or customize instead of starting blank.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which standards is the data model aligned to?</summary>
        <div><p>ISO 55000, ISO 14224, API 653, ISO 50001, and PHMSA 49 CFR 192/195. Aligned to, not certified against.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do assets relate to each other?</summary>
        <div><p>Parent and child links build the hierarchy, from site down to component. Associations link assets outside it, such as a diesel tank and the primary generator it sits beside.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do field crews need signal?</summary>
        <div><p>No. Trek captures inspections offline, timestamped and geotagged, and writes them to the record when the device reconnects.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can we see who changed a record?</summary>
        <div><p>Yes. The audit log keeps who entered what, and what changed since.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

